diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 55a058a..2f3dfa9 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,4 +1,30 @@
-# The $12 Server Challenge
+# BaaS Benchmark Campaign
+
+This fork is being retooled to benchmark the same feed application using each product's supported APIs, one service at a time:
+
+**TrailBase → PocketBase → Supabase → Convex → Nhost → Directus → Appwrite → Neon (if feasible).**
+
+See **[the master plan and progress checklists](MASTER_PLAN.md)** for the application contract, Docker/runner design, resource tiers, correctness gates, benchmark protocol, and per-service publication requirements.
+
+The primary environment is **local OrbStack Docker on this machine**, with **small (1 CPU / 2 GiB)** and **large (4 CPU / 4 GiB)** serving-stack tiers. The owner-approved `k6-2cpu-4g-v2` load runner has a separate 2 CPU / 4 GiB / no-swap container budget, but shares the host/VM. Historical 2-GiB runner attempts are retained separately. Larger-tier benchmarks require a VM headroom review; the current ~8-GiB VM permits small but not large plus this runner and the 1-GiB OS reserve. Managed services and emulated architectures are separate comparison tracks; local results are not the original $12 cloud-VM scores. See the [frozen benchmark contract](contracts/BENCHMARK.md).
+
+**TrailBase is implemented first**, using native WASM routes and TrailBase database/transaction APIs. The full-data golden, concurrency, native API, storage-failure, and restart tests are available; capacity results require the search and confirmation protocol. Each service must have an accepted published outcome before the next starts.
+
+```bash
+bash services/trailbase/run.sh build
+bash services/trailbase/run.sh test
+caffeinate -i bash services/trailbase/run.sh bench --smoke --vus 25 # unscored pipeline check
+caffeinate -i bash services/trailbase/run.sh bench --campaign      # bounded search + confirmations
+bash services/trailbase/run.sh down
+```
+
+See [TrailBase setup and architecture](services/trailbase/README.md) for requirements, resource limits, auth scope, safe lifecycle operations, result locations, and caveats. No other BaaS application has been started.
+
+---
+
+## Upstream reference: The $12 Server Challenge
+
+The original challenge documentation below, along with `SPEC.md`, the seed, tests, and existing submission, is retained as the workload reference. Its SQLite-only rules, submission workflow, and original scoring procedure are historical upstream rules, not the cross-product benchmark policy; see the master plan for planned changes.
 
 How many users can one **$12/month server** (1 vCPU, 2 GB RAM) handle? 
 
